// Forbid Approve if the approver's Submit has NOT been revoked since their Login
// (i.e., the approver submitted something and it hasn't been cleared)
// This uses without-since: !Revoke since Login means "no Revoke since Login" 
// which is true when Login exists and no Revoke happened after it.
// Here: forbid if Submit exists since Login (using positive since would require
// Submit at every point, so we use formerly for the Submit check separately).
// Actually: forbid if the approver submitted the same request (self-approval)
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Approve",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Submit"::request{ input.user: context.input.approver, input.request_id: context.input.request_id }
};
